# Doc Maintenance Protocol

After completing a coding task that changes project state, delegate doc updates to a sub-agent using the Task tool. Do NOT read and update docs in the current conversation — preserve context for coding.

## Required Behavior For "Update Documentation" Requests

When the user asks to "update documentation" (or equivalent), the sub-agent MUST:
1. Apply normal change-to-doc mapping updates.
2. If any roadmap item/action was built, update the roadmap with action-level completion markers (not only phase/group status) using the format defined in `roadmap-maintenance.mdc`.
3. Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md`.
4. Evaluate user-facing impact and update docs in `docs/user-guides/` when applicable.
5. If user-guide updates are not applicable, include an explicit "N/A" rationale in the task report.

## Required Sub-Agent Checklist

The doc-update sub-agent response MUST include:
1. What changed in code/product behavior.
2. Exact docs updated.
3. Roadmap actions marked complete (including completion dates used).
4. Confirmation that `docs/CHANGELOG.md` was updated.
5. Confirmation that user guides were updated, or "N/A" with rationale.
6. "Last updated" date refreshed on every modified doc.

## Sub-Agent Prompt Template

Provide the sub-agent with:
1. What changed (files created/modified, new endpoints, schema changes)
2. Which docs to update (from mapping below)
3. Instruction to update "Last updated" date on any modified doc
4. Instruction to always update `docs/CHANGELOG.md`
5. Instruction to assess `docs/user-guides/` impact and either update guides or return explicit "N/A" rationale
6. Instruction to apply roadmap action-level completion markers (with dates) where roadmap actions were completed

## Change → Doc Mapping

| Change type | Update |
|---|---|
| New/modified API route | `docs/API.md` |
| New/modified Weaviate collection or property | `docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md` |
| New dependency, framework change, or arch decision | `docs/TECH_DECISIONS.md` |
| Content type or context assembly change | `docs/BUSINESS_LOGIC.md` |
| Feature completed or module status changed | `docs/SCOPE.md` |
| New functional requirement or module definition | `docs/PRD.md` |
| New roadmap group | Create `docs/roadmap/group-{letter}.md`, add row to status table and Remaining Work table in `docs/roadmap/README.md` (see `roadmap-maintenance.mdc`) |
| Existing group status changed (e.g., completed) | Update status in `docs/roadmap/README.md` status table, update group file heading |
| Group item completed or modified | Edit the specific `docs/roadmap/group-{letter}.md` |
| Phase-level or cross-cutting change | `docs/roadmap/README.md`, `docs/roadmap/phase-2.md`, `docs/roadmap/phase-3-backlog.md`, or `docs/roadmap/cross-cutting.md` as appropriate |
| New deferred scope | `docs/roadmap/deferred.md` |
| Any documentation update request | `docs/CHANGELOG.md` (prepend, newest first) — required every time docs are updated |
| Any documentation update request | Evaluate `docs/user-guides/<feature>.md`; update if user-facing behavior changed, otherwise record explicit "N/A" rationale |
